# Introducing InstructLab

[InstructLab](graphics/communitydrivenproject.png)

Large Language Models are the new representation of data insights, however, they are only as knowledgeable as the information they contain.  We are a data driven world and new informaiton is generated by the second.  In terms of organisations and enterprised, data is held internally, so to make maximum use of an LLM these organisations need to add their private/propriatory data to their private LLM.  However, it has been a challenge to  customized or tailor LLMs.  InstructLab is here to overcome that challenge and more. 

InstructLab allows for a prescriptive approach to LLM development, where an individual can determine what a model knows and what it can do using a taxonomy.

Prior to our work, it was believed that new knowledge can only be introduced via pre-training, which is super expensive. To resolve this issue we introduced a multi-phased, large-scale alignment tuning that allows you to introduce the knowledge in the dataset we created in a day using only 8 GPUs.

InstructLab is an open-source project, so not only can you contribute to the development of InstructLab, but you can also contribut to the ongoing development of LLMs in a governed manner.

Before we dive into InstructLab, let's find out how we got here!